# The keys trellis.config accepts, one per line: <key>|<kind>|<default>.
#
# kind is single (one value) or multi (a list, written as the key repeated). A single key whose values
# are a closed set has kind enum:<a>,<b>,...: it reads as single, and this is the one place that lists
# the accepted values, which `trellis doctor` checks the file against. The readers compare the
# rung booleans to the literal false, so yes, on and 1 are not accepted spellings of true. A key whose middle part
# is * belongs to a named subsection: [command "analyze"] run = ... is command.analyze.run. A multi
# key with defaults repeats the line once per default value; setting the key in the config replaces
# all of them. Any key of trellis.config that is not here is a FAIL of `trellis doctor`.
#
# This file is the one source of the keys and their defaults: lib/config.sh reads it, and so does
# everything that reads the config through `trellis config`.

